\name{cellucid_history_share}
\alias{cellucid_history_share}
\title{Share the history as a file}
\usage{
cellucid_history_share(
  viewer,
  chats = FALSE,
  content = "history",
  file,
  include,
  journal = FALSE,
  notes = TRUE,
  results = "include",
  source = "full",
  times
)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{chats}{Conversations kept with the trackers (never with a state). \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{content}{history: the trackers and branches with their values; state: the current state only, without its history (one squashed step "Shared state"); steps: the steps only, no cells or values (a replay plan for any dataset). One of \code{"history"}, \code{"state"}, \code{"steps"}. Default \code{"history"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{file}{The file's name; the dataset's name when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{include}{The trackers to include, each with its branches (its main and shown branches when left out); the tracker in use when left out. A vector or list of a named list (at least 1 item). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{journal}{Recently deleted (never with a state). \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{notes}{Notes and bookmarks (never with a state). \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{TRUE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{results}{Analysis results: include them, or leave them out to compute again on open from their recorded inputs (smaller; always so for steps). Steps only always recompute, whatever is given. One of \code{"include"}, \code{"recompute"}. Default \code{"include"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{source}{full: the dataset's name and where it opens from; name: its name only. One of \code{"full"}, \code{"name"}. Default \code{"full"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{times}{exact; dates (each rounded down to its day); none. When left out: exact for a history or steps, none for a state. One of \code{"exact"}, \code{"dates"}, \code{"none"}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{bytes}, \code{content}, \code{file}, \code{steps} (Steps written), \code{trackers}.
}
\description{
Write a session file to share: the history (trackers and branches chosen; the tracker in use, its main and shown branches by default), the current state only, or the steps only; with or without notes, conversations, Recently deleted, times and where the dataset opens from.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.share} (History). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (writes-file); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_share(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
